From 561ca4b7b51e7d05fae45cc09fa2525fad17a860 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 20:45:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] feat: waiting that has the shape of the page, and a board
 with no domain

The portal's loading state was a spinner centred in a 50vh box: the
content vanished, the document height changed, the scroll jumped, and a
moment later everything came back at a different height. Waiting that
causes layout shift is worse than no waiting. It now draws the three bands
every portal route has -- a short opening, a wide slab, a text section --
at the real proportions, so the swap from skeleton to content does not
move the rule. The shell stays up and interactive throughout; loading.tsx
replaces only the layout's children.

The board primitives are geometry and nothing else. BoardViewport is the
horizontal strip, focusable because a scrollable region only answers arrow
keys when it can take focus, snapping on the phone and free on the
desktop. BoardColumn keeps an empty column on screen with its zero,
because a column is an axis and not a block -- hiding it would say the
stage does not exist, which is a different claim. BoardCard is a slab, not
a card.

They know no status, channel, format, approval, version, item, project or
tenant, and a source guard fails if any of those words appears. They reach
no route, no navigation and no data; the only fixture is synthetic and
lives inside the test that uses it.

Three test files added: the shell, the board, and the source boundaries --
including one that fails if a motion or drag dependency ever appears in
package.json.

